# PostgreSQL Production Readiness Transition Walkthrough

I have successfully executed the PostgreSQL production readiness roadmap. All direct SQLite3 connections in the UstadG backend have been cleanly transitioned to dialect-agnostic SQLAlchemy connections.

Here is a summary of the accomplishments and fixes:

---

## 🛠️ Key Improvements & Bug Fixes Delivered

### 1. Dynamic Database Mapping & SQLite Thread Safety
- **File:** [database.py](file:///b:/hackathone0-ai-employee/Ustad-G-project-hacathone/Backend/app/db/database.py)
- **Improvement:** Exposed a synchronous engine (`sync_engine` and `SyncSessionLocal`) alongside the async engine to support sync tasks (like ADK session persistence and orchestrator queries).
- **Critical Thread Safety Fix:** Conditionally passed `connect_args={"check_same_thread": False}` when running on a local SQLite database URL. This prevents runtime thread crashes during parallel FastAPI request handling.

### 2. Auto-Bootstrapping for clean PostgreSQL database
- **File:** [init_db.py](file:///b:/hackathone0-ai-employee/Ustad-G-project-hacathone/Backend/app/db/init_db.py)
- **Critical Fix:** Added `ChatSession` model registration so that the `chat_sessions` database table is automatically created by `Base.metadata.create_all`.

### 3. Fully Database-Agnostic Session Persistence
- **File:** [session_service.py](file:///b:/hackathone0-ai-employee/Ustad-G-project-hacathone/Backend/app/db/session_service.py)
- **Improvement:** Replaced direct `sqlite3` cursors with SQLAlchemy. Used `db_session.merge()` for robust, dialect-agnostic UPSERT behavior. Utilized safe context managers (`with SyncSessionLocal() as db_session:`) to guarantee database sessions are cleanly rolled back/closed.

### 4. Refactored Local Search Tool
- **File:** [local_search.py](file:///b:/hackathone0-ai-employee/Ustad-G-project-hacathone/Backend/app/tools/local_search.py)
- **Improvement:** Refactored `search_local_providers` to run SQLAlchemy queries against the `Provider` model, keeping exact downstream JSON schema compatibility.

### 5. Swarm Agent Personalization Refactor
- **File:** [orchestrator.py](file:///b:/hackathone0-ai-employee/Ustad-G-project-hacathone/Backend/app/agents/orchestrator.py)
- **Improvement:** Replaced `sqlite3` calls with context-managed SQLAlchemy queries retrieving saved user locations.

